        "evidence": "borromean-topological-confinement.md:17-20 'the empirical fact that quarks are never observed in isolation is exactly the Brunnian property of B_3, with no separate dynamical assumption required.'",
        "notes": "This identifies QCD color confinement with a purely topological (Brunnian) property and claims 'no separate dynamical assumption required'. That is far stronger than the construction supports: confinement in QCD is a dynamical (linear potential / area-law) phenomenon with an energy scale; a topological non-separability statement about a link diagram does not, by itself, reproduce the energetics or the gauge-theoretic mechanism. The block itself concedes the energetics live elsewhere (lines 22-28), so the 'no dynamical assumption required' phrasing overclaims. Mitigated as a remark, but the equivalence claim ('is exactly') is too strong."
      }
